course: dictionary
lesson: 16031
title: Veracity: how true something is
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Veracity is a formal word, the kind you meet in news reports, in courts of law and in serious writing. It means truth, or how accurate something is: whether it really happened the way it is told. «We could not confirm the veracity of the claim.» That means the news team could not prove the claim was true.
explain: Veracity can also mean the habit of telling the truth. «The judge praised the witness for her veracity.» Here the word describes the person: she tells the truth. Everyday speech would simply say truth, so when you meet veracity, swap in truth and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The same idea helps you online. «Always check the veracity of what you read.» Before you share a story, ask yourself: is it true, and how do I know? Look for a reliable source, and see whether other trusted places report the same facts.
fact: Veracity is a noun, and it is formal, so you will mostly see it in serious writing.
fact: Veracity means truth or accuracy: whether something is true.
fact: Veracity can also mean the habit of telling the truth.
fact: «Truth» is the everyday word that often means the same thing in a sentence.
fact: Veracity often goes with verbs like «check» and «confirm», as in «check the veracity» or «confirm the veracity».
exercise: «We could not confirm the veracity of the claim.» What does veracity mean here? | *Whether the claim is true | The number of people who heard the claim | The date the claim was made | The loudness of the claim
exercise: «The judge praised the witness for her veracity.» What does veracity describe? | *The witness's habit of telling the truth | The witness's coat | How fast the witness speaks | The length of the court case
exercise: Which everyday word could replace veracity in «Always check the veracity of what you read»? | *truth | pleasure | speed | noise
test: «The news report was checked for veracity before it went out.» What was being checked? | *Whether the report is true and accurate | How long the report is | Who wrote the headline | The colour of the page
test: Which sentence uses veracity correctly? | *The team tested the veracity of the rumour before they believed it. | The cat had great veracity and slept all day. | The rain had a loud veracity. | We ate veracity for lunch.
exam: Ella says veracity is just a fancy word for colour. Why is she wrong? | Veracity means a type of shop | Veracity means a loud noise | *Veracity means truth or accuracy, so it is about whether something is true | Veracity means colour, but only in news reports
